      "body": "For travelers, Tôi quẹt thẻ được không? is the phrase to keep ready for \"Can I pay by card\" in buying small items, receipts, bags, and everyday errands. This comes before checkout if you are not sure cards are accepted. This helps when you do not want to reach the register and stall out. It works best when you focus on letting the other person answer yes, no, or point you to the right option. After you say it, listen for a yes/no answer, a gesture toward the item, or a short alternative; the next rows help you keep the exchange moving.",
